# Throwaway probe scripts.
#
# Driving the app from a script requires Playwright, and Playwright only
# resolves from the repo root — so an audit that wants to EXECUTE the app
# rather than read it has to put its scratch file here. That turned out to
# matter: the defects found by executing (a deload that silently stops firing
# after 6pm, a comeback ease that pins a two-day-a-week athlete forever) were
# invisible to every review that only read the code.
#
# These are scratch and are never part of the app. The real suite lives in
# tests/ and is committed.
/_*.mjs
/zz-*.mjs
/audit-*.mjs
/*.tmp.mjs
# "probe" is the name anyone reaching for a scratch script actually types —
# probe1.mjs, probe-xss.mjs, auditprobe-a.mjs. None of the patterns above
# matched those, so a `git add -A` during a parallel audit swept nine of them
# into a release commit. The glob is deliberately loose for that reason.
/*probe*.mjs
/*.probe.mjs
# Screenshots a probe takes while investigating are the same kind of scratch.
/*probe*.png
/probe*.jpg
